{"id":"21.3.2","doc":"T","title":"HMAC Algorithm Structure","words":223,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The structure of the implemented algorithm in the "},{"t":"block","v":"HMAC","id":"crypto"},{"t":"text","v":" module is shown in Figure 21.3-2."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"This is the standard HMAC algorithm as described in RFC 2104."}]}]},{"t":"fig","src":"images/trm-fig-21_3-2.png","alt":"Figure 21.3-2. HMAC Structure Schematic Diagram","caption":"Figure 21.3-2. HMAC Structure Schematic Diagram"},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"In Figure 21.3-2:"}]}]},{"t":"list","ordered":true,"items":[[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"ipad is a "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" message block composed of "},{"t":"num","v":"64 bytes","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" of 0x36."}]}]}],[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"opad is a "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" message block composed of "},{"t":"num","v":"64 bytes","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" of 0x5c."}]}]}]]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The HMAC module appends a "},{"t":"num","v":"256-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" 0 sequence after the bit sequence of the "},{"t":"num","v":"256-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" key K in order to get a "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" K0."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Then, the HMAC module XORs K0 with ipad to get the "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" S1."}]},{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Afterwards, the HMAC module appends the input message (multiple of 512 bits) after the "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" S1, and exercises the SHA-256 algorithm to get the "},{"t":"num","v":"256-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" H1."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The HMAC module appends the "},{"t":"num","v":"256-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" SHA-256 hash result H1 to the "},{"t":"num","v":"512-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" S2 value, which is calculated using the XOR operation of K0 and opad."}]},{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"A "},{"t":"num","v":"768-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" sequence will be generated."}]},{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Then, the HMAC module uses the SHA padding algorithm described in Section "},{"t":"xref","id":"21.3.1","c":[{"t":"text","v":"21.3.1"}]},{"t":"text","v":" to pad the "},{"t":"num","v":"768-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" sequence to a "},{"t":"num","v":"1024-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":" sequence, and applies the SHA-256 algorithm to get the final hash result ("},{"t":"num","v":"256-bit","k":"size"},{"t":"text","v":")."}]}]}]}